From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] main: stop parking window focus on the shell overlay

Patch 0080 made the shell overlay focusable and the window's focus widget so
F1-F8 capture would survive view switches. That premise does not hold:
capture-phase controllers run from the root toward the focus widget, so the
window, overlay and stack controllers fire whenever focus is anywhere in
their subtree - the overlay does not need to hold focus itself.

Holding it is actively harmful. The overlay is an ancestor of the Casilda
compositor, so while it owned focus the compositor was never the key event's
target and its own key controller never ran: an embedded Activity could not
receive a single keystroke. Leaving focus to real content lets the
compositor take it on the Activity page (see 0136) and lets Home and Journal
focus their own widgets.

This supersedes 0080.

--- a/src/jarabe/main.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/main.py
@@ -366,8 +366,6 @@
             _surface_controller.connect("key-pressed", _capture_zoom_key)
             _focus_surface.add_controller(_surface_controller)
         shell_instance._sugar_zoom_controller = zoom_controller
-        shell_instance._overlay.set_focusable(True)
-        shell_instance._main_window.set_focus(shell_instance._overlay)
 
         if os.environ.get('SUGAR_WINDOWED', '0') == '1':
             shell_instance._main_window.set_decorated(False)
@@ -376,7 +374,6 @@
             shell_instance._main_window.fullscreen()
         shell_instance._main_window.present()
 
-        shell_instance._main_window.set_focus(shell_instance._overlay)
 
 def _start_intro(shell, start_on_age_page=False):
     _setup_main_window(shell)
